s pointer, only bound to type ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"T"},{"type":"text","text":". The closure’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pointer argument is valid only for the duration of the closure’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"execution. If "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"body"},{"type":"text","text":" has a return value, that value is also used as"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the return value for the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withMemoryRebound(to:capacity:_:)"},{"text":" method.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"kind":"parameters"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"return-value","text":"Return Value","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The return value, if any, of the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"body"},{"type":"text","text":" closure parameter."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Discussion","level":2,"anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use this method when you have a pointer to memory bound to one type and"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"you need to access that memory as instances of another type. Accessing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"memory as a type ","type":"text"},{"code":"T","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" requires that the memory be bound to that type. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"memory location may only be bound to one type at a time, so accessing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the same memory as an unrelated type without first rebinding the memory","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is undefined.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The region of memory that starts at this pointer and covers ","type":"text"},{"code":"count","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"strides of ","type":"text"},{"code":"T","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instances must be bound to ","type":"text"},{"code":"Pointee","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Any instance of ","type":"text"},{"code":"T","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" within the re-bound region may be initialized or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"uninitialized. Every instance of ","type":"text"},{"code":"Pointee","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" overlapping with a given","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"instance of ","type":"text"},{"code":"T","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" should have the same initialization state (i.e.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"initialized or uninitialized.) Accessing a ","type":"text"},{"code":"T","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" whose underlying","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Pointee","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" storage is in a mixed initialization state shall be","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"undefined behaviour.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The following example temporarily rebinds the memory of a ","type":"text"},{"code":"UInt64","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pointer to ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int64","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", then modifies the signed integer.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let uint64Pointer: UnsafeMutablePointer<UInt64> = fetchValue()","uint64Pointer.withMemoryRebound(to: Int64.self, capacity: 1) {","    $0.pointee.negate()","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Because this pointer’s memory is no longer bound to its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Pointee"},{"type":"text","text":" type"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"while the ","type":"text"},{"code":"body","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" closure executes, do not access memory using the"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"original pointer from within ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"body"},{"type":"text","text":". Instead, use the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"body"},{"type":"text","text":" closure’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"pointer argument to access the values in memory as instances of type","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"T"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"After executing "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"body"},{"type":"text","text":", this method rebinds memory back to the original"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Pointee"},{"type":"text","text":" type."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Only use this method to rebind the pointer’s memory to a type","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that is layout compatible with the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Pointee","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" type. The stride of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"temporary type (","type":"text"},{"code":"T","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") may be an integer multiple or a whole fraction","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of ","type":"text"},{"code":"Pointee","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s stride, for example to point to one element of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"an aggregate.","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"To bind a region of memory to a type that does not match these"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"requirements, convert the pointer to a raw pointer and use the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bindMemory(to:)"},{"text":" method.","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"If "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"T"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"Pointee","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" have different alignments, this pointer","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"must be aligned with the la